  "sourceInstructions": "<root xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-works/ProductModelManuInstructions\">AI-generated fictional demo instructions. Not validated engineering or safety instructions. Top Tube (Product Number TO-2301) part sheet. Fictional part sheet for Top Tube TO-2301 (product 534), formed from its direct material component.<Location LocationID=\"10\" SetupHours=\"0.2\" LaborHours=\"0.4\" MachineHours=\"0.2\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 10 - Frame Forming. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Forming: prepare and form the supplied sheet into an illustrative tube shape.<step>Check 1.00 EA of <material>Metal Sheet 2 (Product Number MS-0253)</material> for visible damage before forming.</step><step>Use an <tool>assumed sheet-forming jig</tool> to form the sheet into an illustrative tube profile. See <diag>2005341</diag>.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"20\" SetupHours=\"0.1\" LaborHours=\"0.3\" MachineHours=\"0.1\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 20 - Frame Welding. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Welding: demonstrate closure of the assumed longitudinal seam.<step>Hold the formed tube in an <tool>assumed holding jig</tool> and demonstrate welding its longitudinal seam. The seam and method are illustrative assumptions.</step><step>Visually check the seam for obvious discontinuities and set aside any visibly defective piece.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"30\" SetupHours=\"0.05\" LaborHours=\"0.2\" MachineHours=\"0\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 30 - Debur and Polish. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Debur and Polish: clean up and visually check the formed part.<step>Use an <tool>assumed hand deburring tool</tool> to remove obvious burrs from accessible edges.</step><step>Visually check for sharp edges and surface damage, then set aside the completed part for the next operation.</step></Location></root>",
